Here is the root cause:
The function `__ioam6_fill_trace_data()` attempts to retrieve the TX queue from a device even when the packet is received on the RX path (is_input true), using `skb_get_tx_queue()` which does not clamp the queue index. If the ingress device has more RX queues than the egress device has TX queues, `skb_get_queue_mapping(skb)` returns an out-of-bounds index, causing an OOB access to `dev->_tx[]`. Additionally, the call to `qdisc_qstats_qlen_backlog()` is not protected by the qdisc lock, leading to potential data races in concurrent contexts (softirq and process).

